<title>BRAZIL: Brazil IBGE sees coffee cherry crop down 4.72 pct.</title>
<headline>Brazil IBGE sees coffee cherry crop down 4.72 pct.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's coffee crop in 1997 should reach 2.51 million tonnes in cherry, down 4.72 percent from the 2.64 million tonnes produced last year, National Statistics Institute (IBGE) said in a statement.</p>
<p>At the end of April, IBGE envisaged the coffee crop would reach 2.23 million tonnes in cherry.</p>
<p>IBGE, which gave no explanation for the increased estimate, issues its figure in cherry whereas other forecasts are normally in green coffee beans. Agronomists say there is no reliable formula to convert cherry estimates to beans.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
